    countRequired: 'Count required',
    foodCostPctTooltip: 'Ingredient cost as % of revenue, available after all physical closing counts are entered.',
    foodCostPctExplain: 'Food Cost %\n\nMeasures how much of your revenue goes to ingredient costs.\n\nCalculation:\nFood Cost % = (Actual ingredient cost / Revenue) × 100\n\nBenchmarks:\n• Below 30% — Excellent\n• 30–35% — Healthy\n• 35–40% — Needs attention\n• Above 40% — Urgent action needed\n\nThis value updates live as you add sales and stock data.',
    revenueTooltip: 'Total revenue from paid orders today.',
    revenueExplain: 'Revenue\n\nTotal amount from all paid orders for this day.\n\nSource: Automatically pulled from your POS paid orders. Only orders with status "paid" are counted.\n\nThis is the denominator used to calculate your Food Cost %.',
    varianceTooltip: 'Value of the unexplained stock variance after physical counting.',
    varianceExplain: 'Stock variance\n\nThe valued difference between actual consumption from the physical count and expected consumption from sales.\n\nCalculation:\nActual usage = Opening + Received − Physical closing count − Logged waste\nVariance = Actual usage − Expected usage\nValued variance = Σ Variance × Cost per unit\n\nPositive = more was used than sales justify (loss or over-portioning)\nNegative = less was used than expected (counting or sales-entry issue)\n\nNo variance is calculated until every physical count is entered.',
    wasteTooltip: 'Cost of ingredients logged as waste today.',
    wasteExplain: 'Waste\n\nTotal cost of ingredients explicitly recorded as waste (spoilage, damage, expired).\n\nThis is separate from variance — waste is intentionally logged, while variance is the unexplained difference.\n\nCalculation:\nWaste = Σ Waste quantity × Cost per unit\n\nTip: Track waste consistently to identify patterns (e.g., same ingredient wasted every Monday).',
    // Section descriptions
    suppliesReceivedDesc: 'Log all deliveries received today. Each entry updates your stock levels.',
    salesDesc: 'Sales data drives the theoretical ingredient usage calculation. Pull from POS or enter manually.',
    stockCountVarianceDesc: 'Compare consumption measured by the physical closing count with the consumption expected from sales.',
    retrospectiveDesc: 'A quick end-of-day reflection to track patterns over time.',
    // Column labels (variance table)
    colExpectedLabel: 'Expected use',
    colLossLabel: 'Variance',
    colImpactLabel: 'Impact',
    // Variance badge labels
    badgeOk: 'OK',
    badgeAttention: 'Attention',
    badgeProblem: 'Problem',
    // Column header tooltips (short) + explains (long, click to open)
    colOpeningTooltip: "Yesterday's closing stock.",
    colOpeningExplain: "Opening Stock\n\nThe quantity of this ingredient at the start of the day.\n\nSource: Automatically taken from yesterday's closing stock count.\nIf no previous day exists, it uses the current system stock quantity as a best estimate.",
    colReceivedTooltip: 'Deliveries added today.',
    colReceivedExplain: 'Received\n\nTotal quantity of this ingredient received through deliveries today.\n\nSource: Sum of all "receive" stock transactions recorded today for this ingredient.\nLog deliveries in the "Supplies Received" section above.',
    colTheoreticalTooltip: 'What you should have consumed.',
    colTheoreticalExplain: 'Expected Usage\n\nThe normal consumption you should have, based on what was sold today.\n\nCalculation:\nExpected = Σ (Quantity sold per dish × Recipe quantity per serving)\n\nExample: If you sold 10 Fish Burgers and each uses 150g of cod, the expected usage is 10 × 150g = 1,500g.\n\nThis is calculated automatically from your recipes and sales data.',
    colClosingTooltip: 'Quantity physically remaining at the end of the day.',
    colClosingExplain: 'Stock remaining\n\nEnter the quantity that is physically in stock at the end of service, in the unit displayed beside the ingredient. Do not enter the quantity consumed or delivered.\n\nExample: if 4.5 kg of cod remains, enter 4.5.\n\nThis count becomes the next day\'s opening stock.',
    colVarianceTooltip: 'Actual usage − expected usage, after physical counting.',
    colVarianceExplain: 'Stock variance\n\nDifference between actual consumption and expected consumption.\n\nCalculation:\nActual usage = Opening + Received − Physical closing count − Logged waste\nVariance = Actual usage − Expected usage\n\nPositive = you used more than expected (over-portioning, theft, unrecorded waste)\nNegative = you used less than expected (stock count error or missing sale entry)\n\nThe value remains unavailable until the closing stock is physically counted.',
    colVariancePctTooltip: 'Severity of the problem.',
    colVariancePctExplain: 'Impact\n\nHow significant the variance is compared to normal usage.\n\nCalculation:\nImpact % = (Variance / Expected usage) × 100\n\nColor coding:\n🟢 Green (< 5%) — Normal, acceptable deviation\n🟡 Yellow (5–15%) — Needs attention, investigate\n🔴 Red (≥ 15%) — Serious problem, act immediately\n\nFocus on red items first — they have the biggest impact on your margins.',
